course: dictionary
lesson: 3267
title: The many faces of er
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Er» is a hesitation sound, like «um». People make it when they are thinking or not sure what to say: «It's, er, somewhere here.» Writers use it to show a character who is unsure, shy or nervous.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «Did you eat the cake?» «Er… no.», the pause before no makes the reader wonder whether the answer is a lie. A hesitation is a clue, not proof, so notice it and read on.
explain: «ER» is also a short form. In the USA it stands for «emergency room», the part of a hospital that treats urgent injuries; in the UK the same place is called A&E. On old postboxes, ER stands for «Elizabeth Regina», Latin for Queen Elizabeth.
explain: The ending -er is different again. It makes a person who does something, as in «singer», or a comparison, as in «taller». Look at the whole word and its sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: «Er» is a hesitation sound, like «um», used when someone is thinking or unsure.
fact: «Er… no.» can show a character is nervous, shy, unsure, or lying.
fact: ER is an abbreviation for «emergency room» in the USA; A&E means the same thing in the UK.
fact: ER on a UK postbox stands for «Elizabeth Regina», Latin for Queen Elizabeth.
fact: The suffix -er makes a person who does something, like «teacher», or a comparison, like «taller».
exercise: In a story, Ben says, «Er… I didn't touch it.» What does the «er» suggest? | He is very happy | He is about to sing a song | He is reading out loud | *He is thinking or unsure, and may not be telling the truth
exercise: In the USA, what does ER stand for? | *Emergency room | Elizabeth Regina | Extra reading | Early riser
exercise: Which word uses the suffix -er to make a person? | *singer | taller | quieter | faster
test: Mum asks, «What time does it close?» Her friend says, «Er… 6?» What does the «er» suggest? | Her friend is shouting loudly | It is the start of a song | The shop is open all night | *Her friend is unsure of the answer
test: Ella sees ER on an old postbox. What does it stand for? | Early reading | Emergency room | *Elizabeth Regina, Latin for Queen Elizabeth | Accident and emergency
exam: Which word uses -er to make a comparison? | Grammar | teacher | singer | *taller
